{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3054","id":4555537410,"node_id":"PR_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABD4f8Ag","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3054","diff_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3054.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3054.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3054","number":3054,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Preserve Detcore random state through SaBRe bootstrap","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[hermit2, degraded-unresolved, gpt-6-astra, devbig014, role=impl]\n\n## Plain Language Summary and Project Impact\n\nPreserve the random bytes consumed before SaBRe initializes Detcore, so the real root thread continues the same deterministic stream. The loader's authenticated initial random state and completed AT_RANDOM initialization now transfer into the normal Detcore thread; missing proof cannot create a replacement stream. The installer also stages the corrected Cargo-built SaBRe loader, and the landed DBT dependency fixes GNU TLS generation for on-demand clients. These changes address concrete failures on Hermit's path to faithful deterministic Linux execution.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe owned supervisor authenticates the actual image, process generation, configuration, held object bytes and loader phase. Initial transfer, kernel-observed later exec continuation, and supported initial static dispatch use distinct typed results. Ordinary wrapper frames and kernel SIGILL/UD0 stops retain separate proofs. Raw Unix paths and kernel comm bytes are handled without decoding unrelated opaque bytes as UTF-8. Larger original-image snapshots use bounded copying into anonymous read-only file-backed storage; the 128 MiB threshold selects storage rather than rejecting the image. Cleanup stays with the supervisor's owned children, removing the redundant numeric-PID signal after reap.\n\nThe installer now copies the loader from reverie-sabre's bundled Cargo build rather than rebuilding the old SaBRe gitlink. It checks the actual source revision, preserves the one-line sabre.revision format, records the distinct upstream revision, and stages the corresponding SaBRe/libelf licenses. Official artifact paths and backend selectors remain unchanged.\n\nAll 21 active Cargo references and 26 lock source rows now select actually landed Reverie **6ae69f57fa9d675b503f5e631140644e652724ab**. The ten-commit range from b304 includes bootstrap/continuation (https://github.com/rrnewton/reverie/pull/564 and https://github.com/rrnewton/reverie/pull/566), mapping protections (https://github.com/rrnewton/reverie/pull/568), and GNU TLS client generation (https://github.com/rrnewton/reverie/pull/569). That lineage also contains KVM proc/fdinfo behavior, ordered guest-log facilities and lifecycle/RPC cleanup, including draining completed connection tasks and checked IDs. The final main base already selects596b and its entire KVM subtree equals retained6ae, so these facts are not presented as a newly introduced KVM change or runtime certification by this pin. Parent and nested gitlinks are unchanged.\n\nThe final DBT change adds GNU-only `-mtls-dialect=gnu` to the on-demand client producer, matching the installed producer and avoiding unsupported TLSDESC relocations. The full DBT subtree and client flags therefore differ. The DynamoRIO SDK key inputs remain equal; both ledgers explicitly preserve the existing 16-job and 1050-effective-job-second policy on that narrower evidence. No depth assertion or failure status is suppressed.\n\n## Determinism\n\nEarly random requests use the shared Detcore Pcg64Mcg implementation, including flag validation, draw consumption and partial-memory-fault behavior. Versioned image/configuration/generation-bound state is consumed exactly once into a virgin root. The transfer neither replaces ThreadState nor imports unrelated clocks or scheduler metadata. Completed initial auxv initialization is recorded once without drawing or emitting it again later. Exec continuation carries no RNG state and requires the owned EXEC event. Missing or stale evidence remains an error.\n\nThis does not establish complete early syscall/clock accounting or universal cross-backend parity. Existing strict comparisons, guest commands and runtime limits remain mandatory.\n\n## Linux Semantics\n\nObject proof retains held FD/device/inode, root-relative canonical/no-follow path, complete original bytes, exact frame/instruction identity and process generation. Original vDSO bytes are captured before loader rewriting; absence needs maps/auxv agreement. Corrected upstream mapping code restores original PROT bits rather than mixing mapping flags into permissions. The public libc getrandom detour forwards transparently; rewritten syscalls remain the entropy routing boundary, with actual callback forwarding controls covering both caller domains.\n\nRemaining limits are explicit: large snapshots require supported Btrfs/ext/XFS cache backing and available OS/storage/address resources; filesystem type does not prove physical disk backing. Repeated complete-object authentication has a cost. Collisions with the private prctl refuse fatally, and intervening signal/syscall events can invalidate saved SIGILL proof. Complete static/exec/shebang and Linux signal compatibility remain unproven.\n\n## Validation\n\nAt frozen **c961f85503dee4629c00981a7707afe39da71a3e**, the normal merge incorporates actually landed main cdf828d while preserving the reviewed consumer and actual6ae dependency. Incoming main repairs ordinary descriptor-reuse inode identity and KVM actual mount provenance, and puts the existing descriptor fixture in its owned temporary working directory. All fourteen real conflict resolutions are retained. Cargo/lock references keep the newer landed6ae; both historical and current budget explanations remain truthful.\n\nActual locked compilation and final Nextest enumeration measured **664 Hermit methods including every original630 and prior660**, **all six original SaBRe methods**, **681 Detcore methods**, and **508 regular methods**. Exactly four landed KVM configuration methods account for660→664. The four new native configuration methods and two affected existing stdio metadata methods actually passed. The extended CLI descriptor guest fixture was not executed in these checks. No original guest identity, acceptance oracle, filter or numeric runtime limit was dropped.\n\nThe source check scope completed0 in166.517 seconds with4CPU/8GiB/zero swap/1024 tasks. Actual all-target/all-feature workspace Clippy passed in11.250 seconds, together with fmt, pin/budget/refusal controls, shell syntax and generated-DAG checks. Peak memory reached8GiB with36,290 memory-max pressure events and zero OOM or task-limit event. The normal merge commit/hooks passed; all1,728 committed bytes/modes are bound to the final checked source checkpoint. Binary metadata still names precommit8a982+dirty; the official producer must establish committed-head prepared artifact authority.\n\nEarlier exact-source native evidence remains attached to its historical execution: the strengthened public-getrandom forwarding method,29 parser/snapshot methods, two real per-worker-TID raw-comm controls, and two exact installer helper controls against the actual6ae dependency. Installer helper/package evidence verifies required loader symbols, source revision and licenses, not a complete release installation. The unchanged controls were not rerun merely to obtain a new commit hash. The two newly authored valid-path refusal criteria were explicitly replaced with valid-path acceptance and wrong-object controls. Earlier compile/collector failures remain recorded.\n\nThe independent exact-head [Codex source/component review](https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3054#issuecomment-5712268469) approves c961 with explicit runtime limits. Actual independent Claude review of **c961** is still running. The earlier8a982 approvals remain historical, and the original refusal5710517195 was retired by its original issuer at https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3054#issuecomment-5711978105; that retirement is preserved, not republished as a new c961 approval.\n\nThe coordinator's official selected **664+6** attempt at c961 is currently active and explicitly off-record, using the original12-node closure and unchanged9,600 summed node-wall/10,800 whole-run bounds. No result, original DBT echo/true success, original-six success or canonical green claim is made. Latest retained canonical full run remains1838 at158a89f6, FAILED/NOT-VALIDATED with69 successful and10 unsuccessful node outcomes, completed2026-09-17 07:31 UTC. These historical full-run failures are not a new result at this head.\n\n## Relationship to gVisor\n\nThe carried KVM work concerns Hermit's namespace and guest-descriptor identity adapter; it does not replace gVisor's syscall implementation or certify new KVM runtime coverage here. The exact reverie-kvm subtree is identical between main's596b and retained6ae dependencies. Existing ptrace comparisons remain the required behavior reference.\n\n## Human Review Required\n\n**Triggers 2 and 3:** syscall-interception/bootstrap core abstraction and deterministic initial-state transfer. Human review follows the owner's post-facto P0 repair policy. This remains a draft pending the second exact-head review family and assessment of actual guest evidence. The source coauthor relays the independent report with attribution and does not self-attest or withdraw another reviewer's refusal.\n\nTask: hermit-main-tip-d0b1468b-not-validated-22-nodes-mostly-exit-2; owner dev-hermit. Final source evidence: assigned consumer slot `ignored/sabre-random-bootstrap-pin-20260917/merge-main-cdf-1/final-1`, main-relative patch SHA256 `2c26b8b3cb43706fb9250e1e5645a41ae204c74dfcd1aa3314547a673e456b0c`.\n","created_at":"2026-09-17T06:44:54Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T09:42:50Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"abdff198b297734528a08be6597e6c35ca03459b","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":11603596200,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAACs6DTqA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/labels/post-facto-human-review","name":"post-facto-human-review","color":"FFA500","default":false,"description":"Landed under post-facto protocol; needs human review","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11681812195,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAACuEpO4w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/labels/adversarial-review-codex1","name":"adversarial-review-codex1","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Codex adversarial review round 1 completed","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11681812218,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAACuEpO-g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/labels/adversarial-review-claude1","name":"adversarial-review-claude1","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Adversarial review pass, claude lane (round 1)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11684277015,"node_